# Measurement quality gates (no easy relax)

When nightly or dashboard CI fails on measurement-quality gates, **fix the measurements or harness** — do not relax checks unless the user **explicitly** says to.

## Protected gates

Never weaken, skip, or bypass without explicit user approval:

| Script | What it guards |
|--------|----------------|
| `scripts/check-summary-measurement-quality.py` | Min sample runs; Li vs competitor rep parity |
| `scripts/check-summary-skip-budget.py` | Skip-row budget on committed summary |
| `scripts/check-dashboard-invariants.py` | Catalog/summary/dashboard regression invariants |
| `scripts/check-summary-measurement-coverage.py` | Measured-row coverage on summary |
| `scripts/check-merged-multi-os-csv.py` | Multi-OS CSV merge integrity |
| `scripts/check-summary-multi-os-measured.py` | Per-OS measured coverage |

Also protected: **Dashboard invariants** steps in `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `pages.yml`, and `benchmark-nightly.yml` (`publish-dashboard`).

## Forbidden without explicit user say-so

- Raising thresholds, adding allowlists, env bypass flags, or profile-specific exemptions
- `continue-on-error`, commenting out checks, or removing jobs to get green
- Treating `bench_profile=fast` or nightly speed work as justification to lower measurement bar
- Suggesting "relax the gate" as the default fix when `publish-dashboard` is red

## Allowed fixes

- Increase run counts (Li and/or competitors) so parity and `min_runs` are satisfied
- Fix adaptive timing / harness so all languages reach required reps
- Fix ingest, merge, or summary bugs that cause false failures
- Parallelize CI (more workers) without cutting reps or gates

## Escalation

Explain the failure with evidence, propose measurement/harness fixes first. **Ask the user before** any PR that weakens a gate — see also `docs/dashboard/INVARIANTS.md`.
